Description: drm: Scan out an output's own buffer unless it is the second of a stereo pair
 The second output of a pair to present scans out the first one's
 buffer, set with setSharedPrimaryBuffer(). Nothing cleared it again:
 after unpairing, or when the outputs presented in the other order, the
 output kept scanning out a stale buffer of its partner.
 .
 Clear it each time an output presents; the second output of a pair gets
 the first one's current buffer again right after.
